# Start

@set playerName=""
@set playerSex=""
@set maxAffinity=0

@bg Apartment_Bedroom_Morning time:1.5
@bgm Morning fade:2.0

@phoneOff
...

Phone: 06:00

...

A short vibration comes from the fitness tracker.

...

The protagonist opens {him} eyes.

Protagonist: Already?

...

Protagonist: Alright.

The protagonist calmly turns off the alarm.

Without any unnecessary movements, {he} gets out of bed.

@bg Home_Gym time:1.2

A few minutes later.

The screen rapidly cuts between scenes.

Dumbbells.

Pull-ups.

A treadmill.

Stretching.

Nothing unusual.

Just another morning.

@sfx Bracelet

Bracelet: Workout complete.

Bracelet: All indicators are within the normal range.

Protagonist: Great.

Protagonist: Now I can be lazy with a clear conscience.

@bg Kitchen_Morning time:1.2

The coffee machine quietly finishes brewing.

The protagonist pours some coffee.

A diploma lies on the table.

Red.

Several congratulatory envelopes lie beside it.

The protagonist puts the mug on top of the diploma like it's a coaster.

Protagonist: Nice.

...

Protagonist: Five years...

Protagonist: And all for a coaster like this.

The protagonist smiles.

Protagonist: At least it's useful for something.

The computer in the next room makes a short sound.

@sfx Mail

Protagonist: Hmm?

@bg Home_PC time:1.4

The monitor is already on.

There is one new email on the screen.

Sender [br]System: Government Program "Elysium"

...

The protagonist calmly takes a sip of coffee.

Opens the email.

...

Reads.

...

Scrolls a little further.

...

Finishes reading.

...

Protagonist: Four days early.

...

Email: Congratulations!

Email: Based on the results of the comprehensive graduate evaluation, you have been invited to participate in the government program "Elysium."

Email: Please confirm your personal information to continue.

@input playerName "Enter your name"

@if playerName=="" goto:DefaultName else:ContinueName

# DefaultName

@set playerName="Alex"
@goto ContinueName

# ContinueName

System: Name confirmed.

@choice "Male" goto:Male | "Female" goto:Female

# Male

@set playerSex="male", he="he", him="him", past="", novy="newcomer"
@goto ContinueData

# Female

@set playerSex="female", he="she", him="her", past="a", novy="newcomer"
@goto ContinueData

# ContinueData

@phoneOn

@msg chat:family notify:0 from:"Mom" "Where are you? Did school end already?"
@msg chat:exes notify:0 from:"Rin" "I missed you, {playerName}"
@photo chat:exes notify:0 rin/selfie1 sender:Rin

System: Data successfully updated.

{playerName}: Alright...

{playerName}: Let's see.

The contract opens on the screen.

The scroll bar becomes tiny.

...

{playerName} stares at it silently for a few seconds.

...

Takes another sip of coffee.

...

{playerName}: Eighty-seven pages...

...

{playerName}: Not bad.

{he} starts reading.

...

The pages slowly scroll by.

...

Time passes.

...

Finally, the document comes to an end.

{playerName}: Nothing unexpected.

{playerName}: Almost boring, actually.

A large button appears on the screen.

System: Confirm participation.

{playerName} presses it without hesitation.

System: Contract successfully signed.

System: Departure date: in three days.

...

{playerName} looks at the screen for a few more seconds.

...

The phone buzzes.

A message from Max.

@online chat:max contact:"Max 🐶" goto:MaxTalk
@online chat:exes contact:"Rin 🦊" goto:RinTalk notify:0

@waitchat max exes remind:"I still haven't talked to everyone I wanted to."

@goto AfterChats


# MaxTalk

Max: Did you get it already? 😁

Max: Or are you refreshing your email every five seconds again?

{playerName}: Got it.

{playerName}: Told you I would.

@typing time:1.4

Max: WHAAAAAAAAAT???

Max: NO WAY!!!!

Max: I KNEW IT!!!

Max: AAAAAAAAAAAAAAA

Max: CONGRATULATIONS!!!!

{playerName}: Thanks.

Max: NO

Max: NOPE

Max: NOT "THANKS"

Max: THAT IS NOT THE RIGHT RESPONSE

Max: DO YOU UNDERSTAND WHAT JUST HAPPENED???

{playerName}: I got an email.

Max: 😂😂😂

Max: "I got an email," he says.

Max: You were just officially recognized as one of the best alphas in the country.

Max: And you're just like

Max: "Got an email."

{playerName}: Technically, that's exactly what happened.

Max: Sometimes I don't understand how you even function.

{playerName}: Calmly.

Max: Exactly.

Max: TOO calmly.

Max: Remember the graduation exam?

Max: I thought I was going to have a heart attack.

Max: You were sleeping.

{playerName}: I prepared in advance.

Max: SEE?!

Max: EVEN YOUR LAZINESS IS PROPERLY ORGANIZED.

{playerName}: Thanks.

Max: THAT WAS NOT A COMPLIMENT.

{playerName}: Too late.

{playerName}: I've already decided it was.

Max: ...

Max: You know...

Max: Sometimes I really want to hit you.

{playerName}: Get in line.

Max: 😂

Max: ...

Max: Listen.

Max: Seriously.

Max: I'm really happy for you.

{playerName}: I know.

Max: No.

Max: You don't understand how much.

Max: We knew back in school that you'd get picked.

Max: Then university.

Max: Internships.

Max: All those tests.

Max: Every time, I thought...

Max: This is it.

Max: This time for sure.

Max: And every time they told you:

Max: "Please wait until the next stage has been completed."

{playerName}: Bureaucracy values consistency.

Max: 😂

Max: You sound like a professor even now.

{playerName}: I hope not.

Max: Alright.

Max: The important question.

Max: When are you leaving?

{playerName}: In three days.

Max: ...

Max: WHAT?!

Max: THAT SOON?!

{playerName}: Looks like it.

Max: Do they have absolutely no mercy for people?

Max: I'd need a week just to pack.

{playerName}: I don't have that many things.

Max: Because you're a maniac.

Max: Your apartment looks like a museum exhibit.

{playerName}: Makes things easier to find.

Max: I've seen it once.

Max: You even organize your socks.

{playerName}: By purpose.

Max: ...

Max: WHAT DOES THAT EVEN MEAN

Max: BY PURPOSE?

{playerName}: Sports socks.

{playerName}: Home socks.

{playerName}: Everyday socks.

{playerName}: Warm socks.

Max: 😂😂😂😂

Max: You're impossible.

...

Max doesn't write anything for a while.

...

A notification appears.

Max: Can I be honest?

{playerName}: Give it a try.

Max: I'm a little jealous.

...

{playerName}: Of the money?

Max: What does money have to do with it?

Max: Although...

Max: No.

Max: I'm jealous of the money too.

Max: 😂

Max: But that's not what I mean.

Max: It's just...

Max: You've always had a choice.

Max: You could get into the program.

Max: You could refuse.

Max: You could accept.

Max: But me...

Max: I was never even on the list.

...

{playerName}: You knew why.

Max: Of course.

Max: Since birth.

Max: "Beta."

Max: No options.

Max: It doesn't upset me.

Max: I'm used to it.

...

Max: But sometimes you still wonder...

Max: "What if?"

...

Max: Stupid, right?

...

{playerName}: No.

...

{playerName}: I guess...

{playerName}: When you don't have a choice—

{playerName}: It always feels bad.

Max: ...

Max: Thanks.

Max: I don't know why.

Max: But your words always make things easier.

{playerName}: That's because I don't talk much.

Max: 😂

Max: THERE.

Max: THAT'S THE HUMOR.

Max: THAT'S WHAT I WAS WAITING FOR.

{playerName}: I try.

Max: Don't lie.

Max: You never try.

Max: Everything just comes naturally to you.

{playerName}: That's not true.

Max: Yeah.

Max: Tell that to the guy

Max: who watched you

Max: win the university olympiad

Max: after spending three evenings preparing.

{playerName}: Four.

Max: OH WOW.

Max: MY APOLOGIES.

Max: FOUR WHOLE EVENINGS.

...

Max: Alright.

Max: Now for something important.

Max: We're getting together tomorrow evening.

Max: Everyone.

{playerName}: Why?

Max: 🤦

Max: Because our friend is leaving.

Max: For half a year.

Max: To the most isolated city in the country.

Max: And nobody knows

Max: when we'll see each other again.

{playerName}: Sounds convincing.

Max: Because it's true.

{playerName}: Alright.

{playerName}: I'll be there.

Max: Just don't pull one of your stunts.

{playerName}: Which ones?

Max: When everyone is sitting at the bar,

Max: you go home at ten

Max: because

Max: "sleep schedule is more important."

{playerName}: It is more important.

Max: I HATE IT

Max: WHEN YOU'RE RIGHT.

{playerName}: Get used to it.

Max: Never.

Max: 😤

...

Max sends a sticker of a happy dog.

...

{playerName} smiles.

@chatend


# RinTalk

Rin: Did you read it?!

{playerName}: Just opened the chat.

Rin: I texted you as soon as I found out.

Rin: I didn't want you to hear about it later.

Rin: You already signed the contract, didn't you?

{playerName}: Yeah.

Rin: Three days?

{playerName}: Yeah.

Rin: ...

Rin: I hate this system.

{playerName}: Why?

Rin: Because they don't even give you time to process what's happening.

@photo chat:exes rin/selfie2 sender:Rin

Rin: Here.

Rin: Now at least you'll remember what I look like before you leave.

{playerName}: You're being dramatic.

Rin: Of course I am.

Rin: Someone has to be.

{playerName}: You know I can't help you with that anymore.

Rin: I know.

Rin: I just wanted to talk.

...

Rin: Are you free tomorrow evening?

{playerName}: I think so.

Rin: Then I'll see you.

Rin: Don't disappear before then.

@chatend


# AfterChats

@offline

...

The room becomes quiet.

...

{he} opens the email again.

For a few seconds, {he} looks at the national emblem.

...

Then {he} turns toward the window.

@bg Apartment_Window_Morning time:1.5

Beyond the glass, the city goes on as usual.

Buses.

Pedestrians.

Someone is rushing to work.

Someone is walking their dog.

For them, today is no different from yesterday.

...

{playerName} takes the last sip of the now cold coffee.

{playerName}: Looks like...

...

{playerName}: My peaceful life is over.

@stopBgm fade:2.5

@fadeOut time:2.0

...

System:
CHAPTER 0

...

System:
The Last Peaceful Morning

@goto 01_journey_start_RUS.Start